      <h2 class="mt-1.5 font-display text-2xl font-black leading-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white sm:mt-2 sm:text-3xl">Our Grading System</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="max-w-4xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 sm:text-base sm:leading-7">
      Our grading system was built from scratch after the 2026 NFL Draft by Ryan McWalter and Aleks Ryabinkin with the goal of formulizing our process and generating more objective grades, opposed to using scales that are completely arbitrary. We wanted to create a way to streamline our grades between us. The foundation and functionality was coded in Python by Ryan, with the specifics of position traits, archetypes, and weights by trait being a continuous work in progress by both Ryan and Aleks. Ryan also developed a fully functioning draft board template as an Excel workbook, with the entire grading structure built in with additional information and descriptions. If interested in learning more about this process, internal structure, or want access to the Excel workbooks, reach out to Ryan by any contact method listed on the about us page (Email, X, LinkedIn preferred).
    </p>
